Package: csemIRT
Title: Bootstrap-Validated Conditional Standard Errors of Measurement for Polytomous IRT Models
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("First", "Last", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "corresponding@email.com")
Description: Estimates the conditional standard error of measurement (CSEM)
    and conditional reliability for unidimensional polytomous item response
    theory models: the graded response model (Samejima, 1969), the
    generalized partial credit model (Muraki, 1992), the partial credit model
    (Masters, 1982), and the graded and Rasch rating scale models. All
    profiles are expressed on a common standardized latent metric so that
    models that fix the latent variance and models that estimate it are
    directly comparable. Sampling uncertainty of the CSEM profile is
    quantified by parametric or nonparametric bootstrap bands and by a
    delta-method approximation, and a paired bootstrap tests pointwise
    whether competing models imply different measurement precision.
    Further functions identify the latent-trait regions that meet a target
    conditional reliability and visualize all results. Estimation relies on
    'mirt' (Chalmers, 2012).
